{"study_accession":"PRJNA1194206","secondary_study_accession":"SRP549439","title":"THSB1-Positive Monocytes and Pro-Inflammatory Immune Microenvironment as Drivers of Osteoclastogenesis in Postmenopausal Osteoporosis","description":"Postmenopausal osteoporosis (PMOP) is driven by an imbalance in the interaction among osteoclasts, osteoblasts, and immune cells within the bone marrow microenvironment. However, detailed single-cell transcriptomic data on the bone microenvironment of PMOP patients are lacking. This study characterized the cellular landscape of the bone marrow in PMOP and identified key osteoclastogenic pathways. Single-cell RNA sequencing of bone marrow cells from 10 PMOP patients and 10 controls (93,867 cells) was performed, complemented by histological validation and in vitro modulation of key pathways.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":20,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN45174169","study_accession":"PRJNA1194206","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"sample","title":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","description":"Single-cell Sequencing of Bone Marrow","sex":"female","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2024-12-08","attributes":[["isolate","Shandong Provincial Hospital affiliated to Shandong First Medical University"],["age","48"],["biomaterial_provider","Pro. Mingjie Kuang"],["collection_date","2020-08-05"],["geo_loc_name","China: jinan"],["sex","female"],["tissue","Spine"],["sample_type","Case set"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR31611493","experiment_accession":"SRX26976090","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":11708762,"base_count":3512628600,"first_public":"2024-12-08","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: F01"}],"labels":[]},{"sample_accession":"SAMN45174170","study_accession":"PRJNA1194206","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"sample","title":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","description":"Single-cell Sequen